{"id":"M2L1-E05","prompt":"A program should calculate simple interest and the final amount using P=1000, R=10 percent, and N=5 years. Write or describe the calculations for SI and A, give their values, and explain how an f-string can display N and A in a sentence.","marks":5,"responseType":"applied calculation","expectedAnswer":"SI=round(P*N*(R/100),2)=500.0; A=P+SI=1500.0. An f-string such as `f'Amount after {N} years = {A}'` inserts the values inside braces into the output string.","rubric":[{"criterion":"Uses the simple-interest formula with rate divided by 100","points":1},{"criterion":"Calculates SI as 500 (or 500.0)","points":1},{"criterion":"Calculates final amount A as 1500 (or 1500.0)","points":1},{"criterion":"Explains braces in an f-string substitute values","points":1},{"criterion":"Gives a suitable formatted output example or description","points":1}],"source":"PDF p. 29; 1_variables_and_operators.md, Putting it together and f-strings","operation":"apply a formula and describe formatted output"},
